0. Definitions

   "Program" is a program written in the built-in programming language
   of the Engine (the BASIC dialect that the Engine tokenizes, compiles
   and runs), in any form: as a text listing (.bas), as a tokenized file
   (.e99), or embedded in an executable, together with the data files
   that it uses.

   "Runtime" is the part of the Engine that the BUILD statement binds
   into an executable: the object file engine1999.o and the library
   engine.lib, built from the source code of the Engine, together with
   the data they contain (for example the fonts).

   "Standalone Executable" is an executable file that the BUILD statement
   of the Engine created from a Program, or that an equivalent process
   created, if that process does no more than link the Program and the
   Runtime with the system libraries.


1. Programs

   A Program is not a work based on the Engine. The GPLv3 does not apply
   to it, and its author may license it under any terms, including terms
   that do not give anybody access to its source. This also holds for the
   demo programs of the Engine, which are free for everybody to use,
   copy, change and build into executables.


2. Standalone Executables

